.TH FIONA 1 "September 2026" "fiona 1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fiona \- generate file metadata trees and commit them to Git
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fiona
.B -i
.I INPUT_DIR
.B -o
.I OUTPUT_DIR
[
.B -m
.I MESSAGE
]
[
.B -s
.I STATS
]
.PP
.B fiona
.B -v
.PP
.B fiona
.B --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fiona
recursively scans an input directory, collects file metadata, and writes one
metadata file per input file into an output directory.
.PP
The output directory preserves the same relative directory structure and file
names as the input directory. Each output file contains JSON metadata for the
corresponding input file.
.PP
The output directory is also managed as a Git repository. On the first run,
.B fiona
initializes the repository and creates the first commit with the message
.BR "Initial commit" .
On later runs, it updates changed metadata files, removes stale metadata files,
and commits changes using the message passed with
.BR --message ,
or
.B "Update file properties"
by default.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -i , " --input "
Input directory to scan. This option is required.
.TP
.BR -o , " --output "
Output directory where metadata files, statistics, and the Git repository are
created. This option is required.
.TP
.BR -m , " --message "
Commit message for update commits. If omitted, the default message is
.BR "Update file properties" .
This option does not affect the first commit, which is always
.BR "Initial commit" .
.TP
.BR -s , " --stats "
Comma-separated list of metadata attributes to write to each metadata file.
Each attribute can be specified by its full name or short alias.
.PP
The default value is:
.PP
.RS
.B path,name,size,changed
.RE
.TP
.BR -v , " --version "
Print the program version and exit. When the project is inside a Git repository,
the version includes the short Git revision in the form
.BR 1+gREVISION .
.TP
.BR -h , " --help "
Show command help and exit.
.SH STATS
Supported metadata attributes are:
.TP
.BR path , " p"
Relative path of the file inside the input directory.
.TP
.BR name , " n"
File name without parent directories.
.TP
.BR size , " s"
File size in bytes.
.TP
.BR permissions , " e"
File permissions in symbolic mode format.
.TP
.BR access , " a"
Last access timestamp in UTC ISO 8601 format.
.TP
.BR modified , " m"
Last modification timestamp in UTC ISO 8601 format.
.TP
.BR changed , " c"
Last metadata/status change timestamp in UTC ISO 8601 format.
.TP
.BR birth , " b"
File birth timestamp in UTC ISO 8601 format, if supported by the platform;
otherwise null.
.SH GENERATED FILES
.TP
.I OUTPUT_DIR/fiona-stats.txt
Text file containing the total number of processed files and their relative
paths.
.TP
.I OUTPUT_DIR/<relative-input-path>
JSON metadata file for the corresponding input file.
.TP
.I OUTPUT_DIR/.git
Git repository used to track generated metadata files.
.SH IGNORED INPUTS
.B fiona
does not collect metadata for files inside these directories:
.PP
.RS
.B .git/
.br
.B .repo/
.RE
.PP
.B fiona
also ignores these files by name:
.PP
.RS
.B .gitattributes
.br
.B .gitignore
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Generate metadata using default stats and default update commit message:
.PP
.RS
.B fiona -i ./input -o ./output
.RE
.TP
Generate metadata using a custom update commit message:
.PP
.RS
.B fiona -i ./input -o ./output -m "Refresh metadata"
.RE
.TP
Generate metadata with selected fields:
.PP
.RS
.B fiona -i ./input -o ./output -s path,name,size,changed
.RE
.TP
Generate metadata using short aliases:
.PP
.RS
.B fiona -i ./input -o ./output -s p,n,s,c
.RE
.TP
Show version:
.PP
.RS
.B fiona -v
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Failure, including invalid input directory, invalid stats option, or Git errors.
